WEBVTT

00:00.230 --> 00:03.360
THE ABYSSAL CAPITAL RULUIATH

00:03.820 --> 00:04.860
Huh?

00:05.440 --> 00:08.610
The entire city is inverted?

00:08.610 --> 00:10.110
That's what makes it possible

00:10.110 --> 00:13.870
for the Abyssal Capital of Ruluiath
to exist down by the seabed.

00:14.200 --> 00:16.370
Moreover, it's not just upside down.

00:17.250 --> 00:20.990
It twisted the very air surrounding the city

00:20.990 --> 00:21.630
and turned it all around.

00:21.630 --> 00:23.540
TURNED OVER
and turned it all around.

00:23.540 --> 00:25.130
TURNED OVER
That's why we can breathe

00:25.130 --> 00:26.970
TURNED OVER
even when we're inside water,

00:26.970 --> 00:28.760
TURNED OVER
and even stones will fall upward.

00:28.760 --> 00:31.340
And the same power created
the fishman zombies

00:31.340 --> 00:33.890
MERMESIS BERGGREN
and those mermaids, right?

00:33.890 --> 00:35.390
LIVING, NON-HUMAN FISH
Yes.

00:35.390 --> 00:38.020
LIVING, NON-HUMAN FISH
The living, non-human fish were "turned"

00:38.020 --> 00:39.060
TURNED
into undead, half-human fishmen.

00:39.060 --> 00:40.770
UNDEAD, HALF-HUMAN FISHMAN
into undead, half-human fishmen.

00:40.770 --> 00:43.730
DEAD, NON-HUMAN FISH
Dead, non-human fish "turned"

00:43.730 --> 00:45.440
TURNED
into living, non-fish mermaids.

00:45.440 --> 00:47.030
LIVING, NON-HUMAN MERMAID
into living, non-fish mermaids.

00:47.030 --> 00:50.990
It overturns all the rules
and twists them.

00:50.990 --> 00:55.080
A supreme being that changes
the rules of the world itself.

00:55.080 --> 00:57.040
That is Ctarnidd of the Abyss.

00:57.830 --> 01:01.250
The Master's power overturns death itself.

01:14.890 --> 01:20.810
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

02:33.010 --> 02:37.970
#45: FILLETING THE DRAGONFISH

02:37.970 --> 02:42.770
"The Master's power
overturns death itself," huh?

02:43.640 --> 02:48.520
Does that mean it won't die
even if we kill it?

02:49.360 --> 02:52.470
Good grief, what an absurd ability.

02:52.470 --> 02:55.530
I doubt just fighting it normally
will be enough to take it down.

02:57.500 --> 02:59.370
With the NPCs present,

02:59.370 --> 03:02.410
I'd like to avoid jumping
into a fight with Ctarnidd.

03:03.330 --> 03:07.630
It'd be great if we could find our
way out of here once I find everyone.

03:07.630 --> 03:12.420
If you wish to make it out of here alive,
you've gotta entertain Ctarnidd.

03:12.420 --> 03:14.090
Entertain?

03:14.090 --> 03:18.930
The Master of the Abyss brings
people like us here not to kill us,

03:18.930 --> 03:22.060
but to stave off its boredom
by watching us struggle.

03:22.460 --> 03:24.180
In other words,
we're just amusements.

03:25.390 --> 03:27.690
What a tasteless hobby to have.

03:28.100 --> 03:31.690
Is there even a stand-up comedy routine
that an octopus would understand?

03:32.190 --> 03:32.690
Huh?

03:33.320 --> 03:35.670
What are those towers in each direction?

03:36.180 --> 03:37.530
Beats me.

03:37.530 --> 03:40.160
But I know there's a "Blocker" in each one.

03:40.160 --> 03:41.580
BLOCKER
But I know there's a "Blocker" in each one.

03:41.580 --> 03:42.660
BLOCKER
A Blocker?

03:42.660 --> 03:47.920
Some bastards with the unique ability
to shut off your powers.

03:47.920 --> 03:51.540
The only one I've heard
about is "Krionaire"

03:51.540 --> 03:54.670
who can seal off
all types of magic.

03:55.090 --> 03:59.300
I bet beating those mid-boss
"Blockers" on each tower

03:59.300 --> 04:02.180
will trigger some kind of event.

04:02.930 --> 04:08.190
I have to say, Araba, you sure know a lot
about Ruluiath, or rather, about Ctarnidd.

04:08.190 --> 04:10.190
Have you been stuck here for a while?

04:10.650 --> 04:12.770
I've wandered around here
for a fair bit,

04:12.770 --> 04:16.040
but this is my first time
actually coming here.

04:17.280 --> 04:23.200
I know the only Merman
who made it out of this place alive.

04:26.290 --> 04:29.290
Apparently,
the man stabbed Ctarnidd's left eye,

04:29.290 --> 04:32.730
and the next thing he knew,
he was out of Ruluiath.

04:34.050 --> 04:35.300
He's my grandfather.

04:36.960 --> 04:38.130
I see.

04:38.130 --> 04:41.050
So your family has a history
with Ctarnidd, huh?

04:41.420 --> 04:44.810
That's about all that I know.

04:45.390 --> 04:48.810
So, how long are we going
to stay here, all conspicuous?

04:49.230 --> 04:53.190
Well, partly because I want to
get a glimpse of the city overall,

04:53.190 --> 04:57.440
but you gotta stay hidden
as you make your way here, right?

04:57.850 --> 04:59.150
Of course.

04:59.150 --> 05:03.070
Because those "fakers"
are crawling all over this city.

05:03.700 --> 05:06.870
That's why I want to hurry
and get out of here already—

05:06.870 --> 05:09.490
Wait, what are you thinking of doing?

05:09.490 --> 05:12.500
If I wanna get found,
I figured sticking out is the best way for it.

05:12.500 --> 05:13.750
H-Hey!

05:14.420 --> 05:15.250
Cut it out!

05:15.250 --> 05:20.590
Anybody here?!

05:21.760 --> 05:23.260
What are you planning?!

05:23.260 --> 05:24.260
Quiet.

05:27.930 --> 05:30.270
Mr. Sunraku!

05:30.850 --> 05:36.650
Mr. Sunraku!

05:37.110 --> 05:39.690
Bingo! Emul responded!

05:39.690 --> 05:41.400
Is now the time for this?!

05:41.400 --> 05:43.490
They're gonna swarm all over us!

05:44.320 --> 05:45.990
Quit worrying.

05:45.990 --> 05:48.360
The mermaids can't sing while on the move,

05:48.360 --> 05:51.020
and the fishman zombies are
as simple-minded as one can be!

05:51.020 --> 05:51.750
You are saying...

05:53.440 --> 05:56.860
If we just keep running at full speed,
things will surprisingly work out!

05:58.000 --> 06:02.260
Mr. Sunraku! Help us!

06:02.260 --> 06:05.510
Hey, Emul!
And you got Stude with you, too!

06:05.510 --> 06:07.930
I'll grab the fishmen's attention!

06:07.930 --> 06:09.270
No, it's not the fishmen!

06:09.270 --> 06:09.850
Huh?

06:09.850 --> 06:11.270
Behind me is...

06:20.860 --> 06:25.410
D-D-Don't just bring a stranger with you!

06:25.410 --> 06:28.780
This wasn't my intention!

06:28.780 --> 06:34.790
Possessed by a limited pool of monsters,
such as Vorpal Bunnies and Catsiths,

06:34.790 --> 06:37.790
there is a skill named
"Random Encounter."

06:37.790 --> 06:41.460
It's a last resort the weak
would cast out of desperation

06:41.460 --> 06:44.550
when faced with danger
they have no chance of overcoming.

06:45.220 --> 06:48.970
It allows them to summon a monster

06:48.970 --> 06:50.310
far stronger than its summoner.

06:50.310 --> 06:51.310
ARCTUS REGALECUS - LEVEL 125
far stronger than its summoner.

06:51.310 --> 06:53.270
And this is the result?

06:53.270 --> 06:56.270
In the end, you just add
more problems to deal with!

06:59.650 --> 07:01.150
Fire on both our head and tail.

07:02.070 --> 07:03.650
This way!

07:18.760 --> 07:20.590
It's got a breath attack?!

07:20.590 --> 07:23.840
This monster better not be as strong
as a Goldy Scorpion!

07:23.840 --> 07:26.410
That is not a monster conjured down here!

07:26.410 --> 07:28.340
I know nothing about that!

07:30.390 --> 07:32.850
So it's summoned from
outside of Ruluiath, huh?

07:35.310 --> 07:38.100
Araba! You remember
the place we rested at?

07:38.520 --> 07:39.610
Y-Yeah.

07:39.610 --> 07:43.110
I'll attract this guy's attention.
You bring these two over there.

07:43.110 --> 07:45.860
What? You plan to battle
that monster all by yourself?

07:45.860 --> 07:48.910
Who is this fish-looking person?!

07:48.910 --> 07:52.910
You're telling me to go with
a fishman?! God please no!

07:52.910 --> 07:54.620
I'm not without a plan, of course.

07:55.050 --> 07:57.120
I'll join up with you guys later.

07:57.120 --> 07:58.370
I'm counting on you, Araba!

08:00.210 --> 08:02.750
All right. Now we're even!

08:02.750 --> 08:05.380
Hey! I'll take that kid on your back!

08:05.380 --> 08:06.610
Hand him over—

08:14.350 --> 08:15.270
What?!

08:15.770 --> 08:17.980
T-This is bad!

08:17.980 --> 08:19.690
I ran out of mana!

08:22.440 --> 08:23.480
Emul!

08:25.230 --> 08:26.860
Bamboo Lightning!

08:34.700 --> 08:36.330
This bamboo...

08:38.290 --> 08:42.750
Eek! They're still coming!

08:45.630 --> 08:48.420
I was wondering what the noise
is all about. Figured it'd be you.

08:53.390 --> 08:55.930
Big brother Ceecrue!

08:55.930 --> 08:58.520
Emul! So you are safe and sound!

08:58.940 --> 09:00.310
And Rust, too.

09:00.310 --> 09:02.020
Finally, I ran into another player.

09:03.860 --> 09:05.900
Don't just stand there talking!

09:05.900 --> 09:08.110
We haven't lost them yet!

09:08.900 --> 09:10.740
Hold on tight!

09:10.740 --> 09:12.280
Y-Yes, sir!

09:12.280 --> 09:13.950
Let's get out of here, guys!

09:13.950 --> 09:15.790
What's that fishman?

09:17.140 --> 09:18.160
An enemy?

09:18.160 --> 09:19.750
Wait, wait! He's an ally!

09:19.750 --> 09:21.670
Can't you tell that from the context?!

09:26.750 --> 09:28.550
It's already back in action!

09:29.050 --> 09:32.010
Smashing through Bamboo Lightning
with such ease.

09:32.010 --> 09:34.010
What manner of foul scoundrel is this?

09:34.010 --> 09:36.560
I don't have the time to go into detail.

09:36.560 --> 09:39.060
Just follow this Merman Araba for now!

09:39.060 --> 09:40.770
I'll take on that guy myself!

09:41.210 --> 09:43.060
You want to engage
this beast by yourself?

09:43.060 --> 09:44.940
That's too reckless!

09:44.940 --> 09:47.150
We should all fight it together!

09:47.150 --> 09:49.280
I don't care, dude!
Just get me out of here!

09:50.440 --> 09:51.860
I have an idea.

09:51.860 --> 09:52.780
What?

09:53.180 --> 09:55.950
I bet that robot you talked about
can handle this!

09:55.950 --> 09:57.910
You just want to gawk at it, don't you?

09:57.910 --> 10:00.540
Sorry, but we can't use it.
It's out of power right now.

10:01.790 --> 10:04.080
Oh... Okay...

10:04.080 --> 10:05.790
It shock you that much?

10:06.230 --> 10:08.550
Listen to me, Rust.

10:08.550 --> 10:13.340
Even if that thing takes me down,
I'll just respawn at our meet-up spot.

10:13.730 --> 10:17.010
But if you die here,
we'll get separated again.

10:17.470 --> 10:19.890
And the other guys are NPCs.

10:19.890 --> 10:20.890
You see what I mean?

10:22.270 --> 10:23.390
Yeah.

10:23.940 --> 10:27.650
If you keep them safe,
I'll show you my robot later.

10:28.110 --> 10:29.650
I'll protect them at all costs!

10:29.650 --> 10:32.900
Man, thank you for being
so easy to manipulate!

10:32.900 --> 10:34.700
Let's get this started!

10:36.530 --> 10:38.410
Mirror of Fading!

10:38.410 --> 10:38.910
MIRROR OF FADING

10:52.590 --> 10:54.050
Mr. Sunraku?!

10:54.050 --> 10:56.720
A-Aren't you scared of that thing?!

10:56.720 --> 11:00.720
How can you still smile while dealing
with this crazy situation?!

11:01.330 --> 11:05.900
If I have to say,
call it a Pioneer's thirst for the unknown.

11:05.900 --> 11:08.980
That's what brought us to this point.

11:09.400 --> 11:10.730
That's all there is to it.

11:13.490 --> 11:14.490
And yeah...

11:15.240 --> 11:18.120
I tried to act cool and roleplay a bit.

11:18.120 --> 11:21.490
But to be frank, it's easy for me
to escape on my own.

11:22.120 --> 11:23.250
But...

11:23.670 --> 11:26.420
I'm actually starting to get an idea...

11:26.420 --> 11:28.230
...of how to beat you.

11:29.210 --> 11:31.460
If you think I'm just your prey,
you're dead wrong.

11:31.460 --> 11:33.360
Remind you that birds

11:33.360 --> 11:34.800
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON
attack and prey on fish!

11:34.800 --> 11:36.010
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

11:37.010 --> 11:39.510
SHANGRI-LA FRONTIER 2ND SEASON

11:45.310 --> 11:47.310
UNBROKEN LIGHTDANCE
Unbroken Lightdance!

11:47.740 --> 11:51.520
I'm dealing damage against
this huge body, but not by much.

11:51.520 --> 11:53.940
It's like a giant ball of tough hide!

11:55.240 --> 11:57.530
And it packs a real punch, too!

11:58.280 --> 12:03.040
Worse, just like the mermaids before,
it can swim in the air like it's water.

12:03.410 --> 12:06.120
Needless to say,
its charges deal a lot of damage.

12:06.910 --> 12:09.420
Even with this horde
of fishman zombies,

12:09.420 --> 12:12.920
it's making mincemeat out of them
just by moving normally.

12:13.350 --> 12:16.090
Furthermore, it's even got
a long-range breath attack.

12:17.070 --> 12:19.430
This monster can move anywhere
and however he wants.

12:19.430 --> 12:22.430
It is pretty hard to deal with.

12:22.430 --> 12:27.020
To the point you can't help but think,
"Man, are you a Unique Monster or what?"

12:27.430 --> 12:31.730
But that only applies
if we were anywhere but Ruluiath!

12:34.940 --> 12:36.070
SHANA-OH POSSESSION

12:38.070 --> 12:39.860
Reason number one:

12:39.860 --> 12:43.910
You might be swimming the air as if
you're flying, thanks to Ctarnidd's absurd power.

12:43.910 --> 12:46.200
But you're not just simply swimming.

12:46.200 --> 12:49.500
Your motions are being affected
by water resistance just the same.

12:49.950 --> 12:54.880
You'd need a decent amount of distance
to accelerate in water with that size.

12:54.880 --> 12:57.380
But we're in a maze-like city.

12:57.380 --> 13:02.010
You can't build much speed getting
slowed down each time you hit a wall.

13:02.010 --> 13:04.180
Even if you try to accelerate
by going upward,

13:04.180 --> 13:07.770
I can kill your speed just
by ducking behind an alley.

13:07.770 --> 13:08.810
You could've killed me instantly

13:08.810 --> 13:09.480
GRAVITY ZERO
You could've killed me instantly

13:09.480 --> 13:11.400
GRAVITY ZERO
if we both were in the water,

13:11.400 --> 13:13.650
but I can move like I'm on land.

13:14.190 --> 13:17.530
Being able to leap off the ground,
I have the advantage of speed!

13:18.070 --> 13:19.280
And reason number two:

13:19.680 --> 13:22.260
That "staggered" motion
you show every now and then.

13:22.780 --> 13:27.160
At first, I thought you were getting
attacked by the fishman zombies,

13:27.160 --> 13:30.040
but you're still doing that
even after they're all gone.

13:30.470 --> 13:33.040
This is just a pure coincidence,

13:33.040 --> 13:36.710
but those fishman zombies' attacks
likely have such powerful poison attributes

13:36.710 --> 13:40.050
that can give someone
as huge as him "poison" status.

13:40.720 --> 13:45.300
He is likely still under the effect of
their poison debuff, giving him DOT.

13:45.720 --> 13:48.720
Man, you really can't let your guard down
against those rotten fish.

13:48.720 --> 13:51.560
I was right not to engage them at all.

13:54.810 --> 13:58.320
That was close.
Guess I drifted too far away.

13:58.860 --> 14:00.530
And one last reason...

14:00.530 --> 14:02.860
This has nothing to do with Ruluiath.

14:02.860 --> 14:03.450
DISARMED

14:03.450 --> 14:05.450
You had a real bad luck.

14:06.370 --> 14:09.500
I happened to be raised by my dad
who's obsessed with fishing.

14:09.500 --> 14:11.500
He taught me more than
I wanted to know.

14:11.970 --> 14:14.210
On how to fillet a fish!

14:23.010 --> 14:24.510
You see now?

14:24.510 --> 14:26.350
It'd be one thing in the ocean.

14:26.890 --> 14:29.430
But here in Ruluiath,

14:29.430 --> 14:32.850
all your abilities aren't nearly
as unfair as Goldy Scorpion's.

14:33.600 --> 14:35.940
All right. Now I've got my method set up.

14:35.940 --> 14:37.730
It's now just a battle of endurance.

14:37.730 --> 14:41.400
Your toughness versus my Ducusram...

14:41.400 --> 14:43.490
Which one will give up first?

14:43.950 --> 14:45.280
It's a showdown!

14:51.910 --> 14:53.410
All these explosions.

14:53.410 --> 14:57.000
Maybe because they all went there,
but there aren't any monsters around here.

14:57.630 --> 14:59.630
Somebody is fighting.

14:59.630 --> 15:01.630
I've got to join them.

15:01.630 --> 15:03.630
I hope Ceecrue is safe.

15:06.760 --> 15:09.430
Ah, Akitsuakane, right?

15:09.430 --> 15:11.350
I finally met another player!

15:11.350 --> 15:12.890
You're after that noise too, Mordo?

15:13.560 --> 15:17.060
How could I not notice
with that much action?

15:17.060 --> 15:21.370
If everyone runs towards it,
we might find each other pretty easily.

15:21.370 --> 15:23.110
Let us hurry, then.

15:23.110 --> 15:24.240
Right!

15:30.830 --> 15:34.330
I'm really sorry, Hizutome.

15:34.330 --> 15:35.460
I promise I will come back

15:35.460 --> 15:36.160
LOG OUT?
I promise I will come back

15:36.160 --> 15:38.960
LOG OUT?
after I've taken care of everything.

15:43.610 --> 15:44.460
Too slow!

15:44.460 --> 15:46.220
FLEET FLOAT

15:46.220 --> 15:48.090
FLEET FLOAT
Going around, laying waste on this city!

15:48.680 --> 15:50.470
You gotta be at your limit, right?!

15:50.970 --> 15:54.100
Hurry up and sink for me already!

16:07.780 --> 16:10.570
H-Hell yeah!

16:10.990 --> 16:13.180
It's finally over!

16:15.290 --> 16:17.790
Thanks a ton, Ducusram!

16:17.790 --> 16:21.960
It was tough as expected,
but your endurance reigns supreme!

16:23.250 --> 16:26.840
Now onto grabbing all the materials!

16:26.840 --> 16:28.970
Ah, look! It is Sunraku!

16:28.970 --> 16:30.220
- Oh?
- You're right!

16:30.720 --> 16:32.350
Mordo and Akitsuakane!

16:32.350 --> 16:33.970
We're back together now!

16:34.470 --> 16:39.980
With all that noise, I figured somebody
was fighting around here.

16:39.980 --> 16:42.480
But what on earth were you fighting?

16:42.480 --> 16:44.440
Well...

16:44.440 --> 16:48.670
I suppose it's somewhat
a giant oarfish that looks like a dragon.

16:48.670 --> 16:50.860
It won't show up here anymore,
so don't mind it.

16:51.700 --> 16:55.830
But thankfully, that battle served
well enough as a signal beacon.

16:55.830 --> 16:58.500
Do you think we will meet
the others if we wait here?

16:58.500 --> 17:01.610
I already met up with Rust,
Emul, and Ceecrue earlier.

17:01.610 --> 17:03.500
I'm having them wait
at a base right now.

17:03.500 --> 17:04.920
I see!

17:04.920 --> 17:06.170
Oh, and Stude, too.

17:06.170 --> 17:08.010
So we're the last ones to arrive, huh?

17:08.440 --> 17:11.300
Oh, right, I still haven't met Rei.

17:11.300 --> 17:13.180
Let's wait a bit more...

17:18.560 --> 17:20.440
What? A new enemy?

17:22.940 --> 17:25.190
No, this is...

17:32.780 --> 17:37.620
The crumbled buildings are all fixed,
like somebody hit the reset button!

17:37.620 --> 17:39.580
Sunraku, what's this?

17:40.040 --> 17:41.540
I don't know.

17:41.540 --> 17:45.170
But if I have to guess, this has to be
another one of Ctarnidd's abilities.

17:45.170 --> 17:46.840
Ctarnidd's?!

17:46.840 --> 17:49.550
That bastard is toying with us.

17:50.050 --> 17:51.870
Brings people like us here not to kill us,

17:51.870 --> 17:54.970
but to stave off its boredom
by watching us struggle.

17:54.970 --> 17:56.680
In other words,
we're just amusements.

17:56.680 --> 18:01.550
Tch, it had its fun, so now time
to clean up the playroom, huh?

18:02.190 --> 18:05.060
Akitsu! So you're safe and sound!

18:05.060 --> 18:06.730
Great to see you too, Ceecrue!

18:06.730 --> 18:09.780
Mr. Sunraku!

18:12.360 --> 18:14.990
You actually beat that monster?!

18:14.990 --> 18:16.620
I can't believe it!

18:16.620 --> 18:18.990
He dropped a lot of material!
It was awesome!

18:18.990 --> 18:21.080
I got some meat, too.
Want some?

18:21.080 --> 18:23.790
It looks pretty light
and tasteless, though.

18:23.790 --> 18:25.500
Rust! Glad to see you oka—

18:25.500 --> 18:28.000
Sunraku. Don't forget our promise.

18:28.920 --> 18:33.760
Sometimes NPCs give better
reactions than her, you know?

18:35.260 --> 18:36.390
Promise?

18:36.390 --> 18:41.100
You promised you'd show me your robot
if I brought everyone here safely!

18:41.100 --> 18:44.520
I told you back then,
but it ran out of energy, okay?

18:44.520 --> 18:46.040
That's fine!

18:46.040 --> 18:47.520
Oh, okay.

18:47.520 --> 18:49.730
All right! Come forth!

18:49.730 --> 18:54.410
This is the Non-Standard
Tactical Bird, Suzaku!

19:03.160 --> 19:05.290
What is this iron bird?

19:05.290 --> 19:07.290
It looks somewhat lifeless.

19:07.290 --> 19:08.460
Is it broken?

19:08.460 --> 19:11.710
I told you.
It ran out of energy.

19:11.710 --> 19:14.220
It's frozen in the
position it crash-landed in.

19:15.510 --> 19:18.100
Glo... Glorious!

19:18.100 --> 19:22.100
This frigidness of metal!
It's so comforting!

19:22.100 --> 19:25.770
They even simulate the touching
sensation of metal! SLF you rock!

19:25.770 --> 19:27.650
Games from Nephilim Hollow's era

19:27.650 --> 19:30.110
compromised a lot on
that kinda stuff, after all.

19:31.650 --> 19:34.740
Wow, it's modeled down to its joints!

19:34.740 --> 19:37.610
Hey, hey! Don't be so rough on it!

19:37.610 --> 19:41.830
Looks like Psyger-0
isn't in this base either.

19:41.830 --> 19:43.450
Eh? Ah...

19:43.450 --> 19:46.260
I figured they'd notice all the noise, too,
so I waited for them.

19:46.260 --> 19:49.710
But they don't seem to be coming,
so I figured they're with Rust and the others.

19:49.710 --> 19:51.500
Nope, I haven't seen them.

19:52.000 --> 19:54.420
Well, I'm sure a player
of Rei's caliber

19:54.420 --> 19:57.260
would notice the Save Zone
mechanic on their own.

19:57.800 --> 20:01.430
Okay, now all of us,
except for one, are here,

20:01.430 --> 20:03.890
I want us to discuss about the future.

20:04.520 --> 20:05.100
UNIQUE CONDITION - ABYSSAL TIME

20:05.100 --> 20:08.850
UNIQUE CONDITION - ABYSSAL TIME
First, we've been given 168 hours

20:08.850 --> 20:10.940
UNIQUE CONDITION - ABYSSAL TIME
to clear this EX scenario.

20:10.940 --> 20:12.900
UNIQUE CONDITION - ABYSSAL TIME
In other words, we have seven days.

20:12.900 --> 20:14.360
UNIQUE CONDITION - ABYSSAL TIME
We need to discuss

20:14.360 --> 20:16.860
UNIQUE CONDITION - ABYSSAL TIME
how we schedule these seven days.

20:16.860 --> 20:21.530
Counting today as "Day 1," tell me
when each one of you can log in.

20:23.540 --> 20:24.370
TODAY: AKITSU - RUS - MOR

20:24.370 --> 20:27.410
TODAY: AKITSU - RUS - MOR
We'll tackle Rei later...

20:27.410 --> 20:29.950
TODAY: AKITSU - RUS - MOR
There aren't many overlaps, but seems like

20:29.950 --> 20:31.790
TODAY: AKITSU - RUS - MOR
we can all team up on the final day.

20:31.790 --> 20:33.420
How about you?

20:33.420 --> 20:36.300
I'd love to log in every day,

20:36.840 --> 20:41.800
but unfortunately, I have somewhere
to be tomorrow and the day after that.

20:42.390 --> 20:44.760
Depending on the situation,
I might stay there longer.

20:44.760 --> 20:47.520
So, yeah, Emul, watch the place
in the meantime, okay?

20:47.520 --> 20:51.400
What?! I have to stay in
this creepy shack all day?!

20:51.400 --> 20:53.940
Hey! Are you going to leave me here?!

20:53.940 --> 20:56.860
I want to get out of this city ASAP!

20:57.400 --> 21:00.110
Sorry, Araba.
Can you watch them for me?

21:00.110 --> 21:02.370
Well, if I must.

21:02.790 --> 21:06.870
Until I find my weapon,
I'll use this building as a base.

21:07.350 --> 21:09.120
You help them too, Ceecrue!

21:09.120 --> 21:10.540
Yes, milady!

21:10.540 --> 21:12.330
Fear not!

21:12.330 --> 21:15.840
So whoever's able to log in will try
to work through the scenario

21:15.840 --> 21:18.970
and we'll keep each other updated, right?

21:19.630 --> 21:22.260
Let's call it out for today.

21:22.260 --> 21:26.900
But I don't intend to give up with
the Master of the Abyss treating us like fools.

21:26.900 --> 21:28.890
Day 7 will be our "X Day."

21:28.890 --> 21:36.020
This time we'll be the one to serve the huge
surprise to Ctarnidd and its absurd ability!

21:36.020 --> 21:37.150
Yes!

21:37.150 --> 21:39.780
Serve it good!

21:39.780 --> 21:43.030
SIX DAYS TO X DAY

23:17.250 --> 23:20.590
Say, since we're here in Japan and all,

23:20.590 --> 23:24.090
how about we tour around
before we go to the GGC venue?

23:25.340 --> 23:29.550
Before that, anyone know
the hotel Uomi Kei is staying at?

23:30.140 --> 23:34.310
Whoa, there. Going to personally
declare war on the guy already?

23:34.310 --> 23:36.330
What's the rush?

23:37.290 --> 23:39.000
Ms. Number #1 in the US.
